@prefix aia:          <https://w3id.org/aia-ont#> .
@prefix owl:          <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:         <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:          <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dct:          <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix skos:         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix eli:          <http://data.europa.eu/eli/ontology#> .
@prefix airo:         <https://w3id.org/airo#> .
@prefix eu-aiact-owl: <https://w3id.org/dpv/legal/eu/aiact/owl#> .
@prefix dpv-owl:      <https://w3id.org/dpv/owl#> .
@prefix org:          <http://www.w3.org/ns/org#> .

#################################################################
#    AIA-Ont worked example
#
#    SEPARATE FILE, IMPORTING THE CORE. The core ontology carries no
#    instance data; anything that wants the example loads THIS file,
#    which imports aia-ont.ttl through catalog-v001.xml. The reason is
#    the same one that keeps the alignment module out of the core: a
#    reviewer loading aia-ont.ttl is entitled to the model without a
#    test fixture in it, and the fixture is the thing most likely to
#    change.
#
#    NAMESPACE. The individuals below are minted in aia:, not in a
#    separate example namespace, because ../queries/ already names
#    aia:ExampleRecruitmentScreeningSystem in two places -- the CQ1
#    reasoner ASK and CQ3's VALUES clause -- and those queries are the
#    specification this file is built to satisfy. Every example term
#    carries the Example/ra_/rr_/rc_/g_/oa_/route_ prefix, so the
#    fixture is separable from the model by name as well as by file.
#
#    ── WHAT THIS FILE HAS TO DEMONSTRATE, AND WHY EACH PIECE IS HERE ──
#
#    (1) ALL FOUR RISK TIERS. Decision 2 in ../reports/STATUS.md brought
#        Article 50's tier INTO scope on the argument that "AI system
#        categories" is a named requirement of the task specification
#        and eu-aiact:RiskLevelTransparencyRequired is the fourth tier.
#        That decision is recorded in prose; without a system at each
#        tier it is not DEMONSTRATED. Seven systems cover Prohibited,
#        High (both Article 6 routes), Transparency-required and
#        Minimal.
#
#    (2) THE DUAL-ROLE ACTOR. An actor holding two roles for ONE system
#        concurrently is the case that makes role-as-class inconsistent
#        and is therefore the whole justification for reifying role
#        assignment. It appears twice and in two different forms:
#        NorthBorough Council holds Deployer and Provider for the
#        recruitment system after Article 25(1)(b) (the Article 25
#        case, which CQ3 is documented to return once per role), and
#        EuroDistribution holds Distributor and Importer for the same
#        system (Recital 83's own example, which CQ3's FILTER excludes
#        and which is here to show the filter working).
#
#    (3) ALL THREE LIMBS OF ARTICLE 25(1). CQ4's note in
#        ../reports/competency-questions.md says the expected results
#        correspond to the three circumstances of Article 25(1), so all
#        three are instantiated, on three different systems and from
#        three different prior roles -- deployer, importer, distributor.
#
#    (4) A NEGATIVE CONTROL ON THE CLASSIFICATION RULE. The chatbot
#        carries a purpose ground and nothing else. Under the classification
#        rule it must NOT be classified high-risk: intended purpose is
#        how one determines whether a system falls within an Annex III
#        use case, not an independent route to the category. If a
#        future edit made aia:PurposeGround a disjunct of
#        aia:HighRiskByGround, this system is what would catch it.
#
#    (5) THE ARTICLE 25(1)(c) DOUBLE TYPING. The disjointness axiom in
#        the core deliberately omits aia:ReassignmentCondition, on the
#        ground that Article 25(1)(c) is simultaneously a reassignment
#        condition and a classification ground. That claim is asserted
#        in a comment and was, until this file, never exercised:
#        aia:rc_art25_1_c_purpose_modification is typed as both and is
#        used in both positions.
#
#    (6) A NEGATIVE CONTROL ON THE ARTICLE 6(3) DEROGATION. The CV
#        formatter falls within the Annex III, point 4(a) recruitment use
#        case but only performs a narrow procedural task and profiles no
#        one, so Art. 6(3) takes it out of high risk. Its ground is an
#        aia:DerogatedAnnexIIIGround, and it must NOT be classified
#        high-risk.
#
#    NOT DEMONSTRATED, DELIBERATELY. There is no deployer for the
#    imaging triage or workforce systems, no natural person as an actor, and
#    no AI Office oversight assignment -- the last because the AI
#    Office's competence over AI systems under Art. 75(1) reaches only
#    systems based on a general-purpose AI model developed by the same
#    provider, and systems that are or are integrated into a very large
#    online platform or search engine. No system here is either. CQ5's
#    AIOffice VALUES row is therefore expected to stay unbound, and that
#    is a property of the fixture rather than a gap in the model.
#################################################################

<https://w3id.org/aia-ont/example>
    a owl:Ontology ;
    owl:versionIRI <https://w3id.org/aia-ont/example/0.1> ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.1" ;
    dct:title       "EU AI Act Ontology — worked example"@en ;
    dct:description """Instance data for AIA-Ont: seven AI systems across all four risk
        tiers, six actors, three authorities, ten role assignments, the three Article 25(1)
        reassignments, and the oversight and conformity-route bindings CQ5 needs. Held apart
        from the core so that loading the core carries no fixture."""@en ;
    dct:creator     "Andreas Chari" ;
    dct:created     "2026-09-26"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:license     <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
    owl:imports     <https://w3id.org/aia-ont> ;
    rdfs:comment    """Resolved offline through catalog-v001.xml. Every organisation,
        system and authority named here is fictitious; the articles, annexes and tiers they
        are attached to are not."""@en .

#################################################################
#    One stub, and the decision it settles
#
#    CQ5 binds  ?authority a org:Organization  and the alignment
#    module records in terms that nothing supplies it: "Whether
#    org:Organization should be the type of the authorities is a SECOND
#    decision, deferred to the authority module; CQ5 assumes it and
#    nothing here supplies it, so CQ5's ?authority pattern will not
#    bind on this module alone."
#
#    TAKEN HERE: the authorities ARE typed org:Organization. The
#    argument for it is thin but sufficient -- CQ5's query is the
#    specification, an authority is an organisation, and the reuse
#    survey already selected ORG for exactly this job (see CQ3 and CQ5
#    under "Reuse" in ../reports/competency-questions.md).
#
#    The argument against was the ORG hazard, and it does not reach
#    this use: what makes ORG dangerous is that org:organization has
#    range org:Organization while it and org:member are FUNCTIONAL, so
#    subclassing org:Membership would identify two systems as one. That
#    is a hazard of ORG's PROPERTIES. No ORG property is used here and
#    none is asserted; only the class is, on individuals, which brings
#    no functional property into play.
#
#    Declaration only, exactly as the core's external term stubs and the alignment
#    module's stubs are declaration only. ORG remains aligned and not
#    imported, so org:Organization would otherwise be an undeclared IRI
#    in class position and the file would fall outside OWL 2 DL.
#################################################################

org:Organization a owl:Class .

#################################################################
#    AI systems, one per demonstration
#
#    Each is an airo:AISystem -- the reuse decisions forbid a local
#    system class -- with exactly one aia:hasRiskCategory. The tier
#    values are eu-aiact terms; the grounds are local, because the rule
#    connecting a ground to a tier is stated in axioms by no surveyed
#    vocabulary and is the classification rule's defined class.
#
#    NOTE WHAT IS NOT ASSERTED. No system is typed with a
#    eu-aiact:HighRiskAISystem-AnnexIII-* or -AnnexI-* class, although
#    those classes exist and would be true of two of them. Typing them
#    would make CQ1's reasoner ASK succeed by re-assertion --
#    -AnnexIII-4-a is already a subclass of HighRiskAISystem-A6-2 --
#    and the ASK would then test nothing. The Annex reference is
#    carried by rdfs:seeAlso on the GROUND instead, so the ASK
#    succeeds only through aia:HighRiskByGround, which is the axiom
#    under test.
#################################################################

### High-risk, Article 6(2) / Annex III — the system every CQ names ###

aia:ExampleRecruitmentScreeningSystem a owl:NamedIndividual , airo:AISystem ;
    aia:hasRiskCategory eu-aiact-owl:RiskLevelHigh ;
    aia:classifiedOnGround aia:g_recruitment_annexIII_4a ;
    skos:prefLabel "TalentFlow CV Screening (example system)"@en ;
    skos:definition """An AI system placed on the Union market to analyse and filter job
        applications and to rank candidates for interview, deployed by a local authority in
        its own recruitment."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """The system named in CQ1's reasoner ASK and in CQ3's VALUES clause.
        High-risk by the Annex III route, and after Art. 25(1)(b) the subject of the
        dual-role case."""@en .

### High-risk, Article 6(1) / Annex I, Section A — the second route #

aia:ExampleMedicalImagingTriageSoftware a owl:NamedIndividual , airo:AISystem ;
    aia:hasRiskCategory eu-aiact-owl:RiskLevelHigh ;
    aia:classifiedOnGround aia:g_medical_annexI_11 ;
    skos:prefLabel "Helvetia MedTech Imaging Triage (example system)"@en ;
    skos:definition """An AI system that is itself a medical device: software that
        analyses chest radiographs and flags suspected findings for priority review by a
        radiologist, classified as a class IIa device under Regulation (EU) 2017/745 and
        therefore required to undergo third-party conformity assessment by a notified
        body."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Present so that the second disjunct of aia:HighRiskByGround is
        exercised by data and not only by the reasoner check's inline fixture.

        WHY A SECTION A PRODUCT. Annex I, Section A lists the legislation to which the
        Act's high-risk requirements and obligations apply in full; for Section B
        products Art. 2(2) applies only Art. 6(1), Art. 60a and Arts. 102 to 112. This
        system bears Art. 16 duties and undergoes an Art. 25 reassignment, so it must be a
        Section A product. Machinery is NOT one: Annex I lists the Machinery Regulation
        (EU) 2023/1230 in Section B, point 21. The notified body's assessment is required
        for health risks, which is what Art. 6(1c) requires of the third-party
        assessment in Art. 6(1)(b)."""@en .

### High-risk by Article 25(1)(c) purpose modification #############

aia:ExampleWorkforceAnalyticsSystem a owl:NamedIndividual , airo:AISystem ;
    aia:hasRiskCategory eu-aiact-owl:RiskLevelHigh ;
    aia:classifiedOnGround aia:rc_art25_1_c_purpose_modification ;
    skos:prefLabel "PeopleMetrics Workforce Analytics (example system)"@en ;
    skos:definition """An AI system placed on the market for aggregate workforce reporting
        and not classified as high-risk, whose intended purpose a distributor then modified
        to the evaluation of individual employees for promotion, bringing it within Annex
        III, point 4(b)."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Art. 25(1)(c). Its classification ground IS the reassignment condition
        -- one individual in both positions -- which is why aia:ReassignmentCondition is
        omitted from the core's owl:AllDisjointClasses axiom."""@en .

### Transparency-required, Article 50 — decision 2's tier ##########

aia:ExampleCustomerServiceChatbot a owl:NamedIndividual , airo:AISystem ;
    aia:hasRiskCategory eu-aiact-owl:RiskLevelTransparencyRequired ;
    aia:classifiedOnGround aia:g_chatbot_purpose ;
    skos:prefLabel "EuroDistribution Support Assistant (example system)"@en ;
    skos:definition """An AI system intended to interact directly with natural persons in
        customer support, neither prohibited nor high-risk, and subject to the transparency
        requirement that the persons concerned be informed they are interacting with an AI
        system."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """The system that discharges decision 2 in ../reports/STATUS.md: the Art. 50 tier
        is IN scope, its obligations are OUT, so this system has a tier and an article and
        no obligations hang off it. ALSO THE NEGATIVE CONTROL on the classification rule -- a
        purpose ground alone must not yield high-risk."""@en .

### Prohibited, Article 5(1)(f) ####################################

aia:ExampleWorkplaceEmotionRecognitionSystem a owl:NamedIndividual , airo:AISystem ;
    aia:hasRiskCategory eu-aiact-owl:RiskLevelProhibited ;
    rdfs:seeAlso aia:pp_art5_1_f ;
    skos:prefLabel "Sentio Workplace Affect Monitor (example system)"@en ;
    skos:definition """An AI system that infers the emotions of employees from video of
        their workstations, outside any medical or safety purpose."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """No aia:classifiedOnGround: the ground hierarchy is Art. 6 apparatus and
        Art. 5 is not a classification route. The link to the practice is rdfs:seeAlso and
        NOT an object property, deliberately: Art. 5 prohibits the practice of placing on
        the market, putting into service or using, not the artefact, and a
        system-to-practice property would re-attach the prohibition to the artefact --
        which is the distinction aia:ProhibitedPractice exists to preserve. The tier is
        nonetheless a property of the system, because eu-aiact models it that way."""@en .

### Minimal, Annex III area but derogated under Article 6(3) #######

aia:ExampleCVFormattingTool a owl:NamedIndividual , airo:AISystem ;
    aia:hasRiskCategory eu-aiact-owl:RiskLevelMinimal ;
    aia:classifiedOnGround aia:g_cvformat_annexIII_4a_derogated ;
    skos:prefLabel "HireDesk CV Formatter (example system)"@en ;
    skos:definition """An AI system that converts job applications received in varied formats
        into a single standard layout for recruiters, without scoring, ranking or filtering
        candidates."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Used in recruitment, the area of Annex III, point 4(a), but Art. 6(3)(a)
        takes it out of high risk: it performs only a narrow procedural task, and it does not
        profile natural persons. THE NEGATIVE CONTROL on the derogation -- a derogated Annex
        III ground must not yield high-risk."""@en .

### Minimal — the residual tier ####################################

aia:ExampleSpamFilter a owl:NamedIndividual , airo:AISystem ;
    aia:hasRiskCategory eu-aiact-owl:RiskLevelMinimal ;
    skos:prefLabel "NorthBorough Mail Filter (example system)"@en ;
    skos:definition """An AI system used to classify inbound electronic mail as unsolicited,
        falling outside the prohibited, high-risk and transparency-required tiers."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Carries no aia:definedIn through its tier, because no article of the
        Act establishes a minimal-risk tier -- it is the residual category. CQ1's ?article
        column is therefore expected to be unbound on this row, and that absence is an
        assertion about the Act rather than a missing annotation."""@en .

#################################################################
#    Classification grounds
#
#    Each carries rdfs:seeAlso to the eu-aiact Annex class it
#    instantiates, following the convention the Art. 5 practices use.
#    seeAlso and not rdf:type: see the note on the systems above.
#################################################################

aia:g_recruitment_annexIII_4a a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        aia:AnnexIIIGround , aia:PurposeGround ;
    rdfs:seeAlso eu-aiact-owl:HighRiskAISystem-AnnexIII-4-a ;
    skos:prefLabel "Intended for the recruitment and selection of natural persons (Annex III, 4(a))"@en ;
    skos:definition """The system's intended purpose is to analyse and filter job
        applications and evaluate candidates, which falls within the Annex III, point 4(a)
        use case."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """DOUBLE-TYPED ON PURPOSE. Art. 6(2) makes a system high-risk where its
        intended purpose falls within an Annex III use case, so one ground is both a
        purpose ground and an Annex III ground. This is why the three ground classes are
        not pairwise disjoint, and why CQ1 returns this ground twice -- once per ground
        type. That is the documented intended behaviour, not duplication."""@en .

aia:g_medical_annexI_11 a owl:NamedIndividual , aia:AnnexIGround ;
    rdfs:seeAlso eu-aiact-owl:HighRiskAISystem-AnnexI-11 ;
    skos:prefLabel "Medical device requiring third-party conformity assessment (Annex I, Section A, point 11)"@en ;
    skos:definition """The system is itself a product covered by Regulation (EU) 2017/745
        on medical devices, listed in Annex I, Section A, point 11, and that product is
        required to undergo a third-party conformity assessment on account of risks to
        health and safety."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Art. 6(1)(a)-(b) and 6(1c); Annex I, Section A, point 11, verified
        against the Official Journal. Art. 6(1)(a)'s "itself a product" limb, so the
        safety-component tests of Art. 3(14) and Art. 6(1a)-(1b) are not engaged."""@en .


aia:g_cvformat_annexIII_4a_derogated a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        aia:DerogatedAnnexIIIGround , aia:PurposeGround ;
    rdfs:seeAlso eu-aiact-owl:HighRiskAISystem-AnnexIII-4-a ;
    skos:prefLabel "Recruitment use case derogated as a narrow procedural task (Annex III, 4(a); Art. 6(3)(a))"@en ;
    skos:definition """The system's intended purpose lies within the Annex III, point 4(a)
        recruitment use case, but it is intended only to perform a narrow procedural task and
        does not profile natural persons, so Article 6(3) excludes it from high risk."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Art. 6(3)(a), verified against the Official Journal. Double-typed as a
        purpose ground, as the recruitment system's Annex III ground is."""@en .

aia:g_chatbot_purpose a owl:NamedIndividual , aia:PurposeGround ;
    rdfs:seeAlso eu-aiact-owl:IntendedPurpose ;
    skos:prefLabel "Intended for direct interaction with natural persons (Art. 50(1))"@en ;
    skos:definition """The system's intended purpose is direct interaction with natural
        persons, which engages the Art. 50 transparency requirement and falls within no
        Annex III use case."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """A PurposeGround and nothing else, which is what makes it the negative
        control: aia:HighRiskByGround has no purpose disjunct, so this ground must not
        classify its system as high-risk."""@en .

#################################################################
#    Actors
#
#    airo:AIOperator, which AIRO sources to Art. 3(8) and which is
#    therefore exactly the set of parties that can hold a role.
#    org:Organization is asserted here too, so the actors and the
#    authorities carry the same organisational type; CQ3 does not
#    require it and CQ5 does.
#
#    No actor is typed aia:Provider or aia:Deployer. Those are
#    INDIVIDUALS of aia:Role, reached through an aia:RoleAssignment,
#    and asserting one as a type would be the modelling error the
#    reification exists to prevent -- the core's disjointness axiom
#    catches it, and the reasoner check has that negative control.
#################################################################

aia:ExampleActorTalentFlowGmbH a owl:NamedIndividual , airo:AIOperator , org:Organization ;
    skos:prefLabel "TalentFlow GmbH (example actor)"@en ;
    skos:definition """The undertaking that developed the recruitment screening system and
        placed it on the Union market under its own name."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Initial provider of the recruitment system; ceases to be so under Art. 25(2)."@en .

aia:ExampleActorNorthBoroughCouncil a owl:NamedIndividual , airo:AIOperator , org:Organization ;
    skos:prefLabel "North Borough Council (example actor)"@en ;
    skos:definition """A public authority using the recruitment screening system under its
        own authority in its own recruitment, which then substantially modified it."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """THE DUAL-ROLE ACTOR. Holds Deployer and Provider for the SAME system
        concurrently after Art. 25(1)(b). Under role-as-class with disjoint role classes
        this single actor would make the ontology inconsistent; under reified assignments it
        is two assignments and CQ3 returns it once per role."""@en .

aia:ExampleActorEuroDistributionBV a owl:NamedIndividual , airo:AIOperator , org:Organization ;
    skos:prefLabel "EuroDistribution BV (example actor)"@en ;
    skos:definition """An undertaking in the supply chain that both imported the recruitment
        screening system into the Union and made it available on the market."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Recital 83's own example -- an operator acting as distributor and
        importer at once, bearing each set of duties cumulatively. Holds two concurrent
        assignments for one system, neither of which CQ3's FILTER admits, so this actor is
        what shows the filter is doing work."""@en .

aia:ExampleActorHelvetiaMedTechAG a owl:NamedIndividual , airo:AIOperator , org:Organization ;
    skos:prefLabel "Helvetia MedTech AG (example actor)"@en ;
    skos:definition """A third-country undertaking that developed the imaging triage
        software and placed it on the Union market under its own name."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Initial provider of the imaging triage software; ceases to be so under
        Art. 25(2), and bears the residual cooperation duties of Art. 25(2) thereafter."""@en .

aia:ExampleActorRhineImportsGmbH a owl:NamedIndividual , airo:AIOperator , org:Organization ;
    skos:prefLabel "Rhine Imports GmbH (example actor)"@en ;
    skos:definition """An undertaking established in the Union that placed the imaging
        triage software on the market and then affixed its own trade mark to it."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Importer promoted to provider under Art. 25(1)(a)."@en .

aia:ExampleActorPeopleMetricsLtd a owl:NamedIndividual , airo:AIOperator , org:Organization ;
    skos:prefLabel "PeopleMetrics Ltd (example actor)"@en ;
    skos:definition """An undertaking that made the workforce analytics system available on
        the Union market and modified its intended purpose."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Distributor promoted to provider under Art. 25(1)(c)."@en .

#################################################################
#    Role assignments
#
#    Ten, each relating exactly one actor, one role and one system.
#    The pattern is the substance of the model: an actor's role holds
#    relative to one system and is contingent on conduct, so it cannot
#    be class membership.
#################################################################

### The recruitment system ########################################

aia:ra_recruitment_talentflow_provider a owl:NamedIndividual , aia:RoleAssignment ;
    aia:concernsSystem aia:ExampleRecruitmentScreeningSystem ;
    aia:hasRole        aia:Provider ;
    aia:heldBy         aia:ExampleActorTalentFlowGmbH ;
    skos:prefLabel "TalentFlow as provider of the recruitment system"@en ;
    skos:definition """The holding of the provider role by TalentFlow GmbH in respect of the
        recruitment screening system, by having developed it and placed it on the market
        under its own name."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Art. 3(3). Terminated by aia:rr_recruitment_northborough under Art. 25(2)."@en .

aia:ra_recruitment_northborough_deployer a owl:NamedIndividual , aia:RoleAssignment ;
    aia:concernsSystem aia:ExampleRecruitmentScreeningSystem ;
    aia:hasRole        aia:Deployer ;
    aia:heldBy         aia:ExampleActorNorthBoroughCouncil ;
    skos:prefLabel "North Borough Council as deployer of the recruitment system"@en ;
    skos:definition """The holding of the deployer role by North Borough Council in respect
        of the recruitment screening system, by using it under its own authority in a
        professional activity."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Art. 3(4). RETAINED after the Art. 25 reassignment: aia:promotes does
        not end the prior assignment, because Art. 25(1) does not provide that the prior
        role ceases. Contrast aia:terminates on the initial provider's assignment."""@en .

aia:ra_recruitment_northborough_provider a owl:NamedIndividual , aia:RoleAssignment ;
    aia:concernsSystem aia:ExampleRecruitmentScreeningSystem ;
    aia:hasRole        aia:Provider ;
    aia:heldBy         aia:ExampleActorNorthBoroughCouncil ;
    skos:prefLabel "North Borough Council as provider of the recruitment system"@en ;
    skos:definition """The holding of the provider role by North Borough Council in respect
        of the recruitment screening system, acquired by substantially modifying a high-risk
        system already placed on the market so that it remains high-risk."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Art. 25(1)(b). Held CONCURRENTLY with the deployer assignment above by
        the same actor for the same system, which is the case the reification exists
        for."""@en .

aia:ra_recruitment_eurodistribution_importer a owl:NamedIndividual , aia:RoleAssignment ;
    aia:concernsSystem aia:ExampleRecruitmentScreeningSystem ;
    aia:hasRole        aia:Importer ;
    aia:heldBy         aia:ExampleActorEuroDistributionBV ;
    skos:prefLabel "EuroDistribution as importer of the recruitment system"@en ;
    skos:definition """The holding of the importer role by EuroDistribution BV in respect of
        the recruitment screening system, by placing on the Union market a system bearing
        the name of an undertaking established outside the Union."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Art. 3(6). Obligations at Art. 23, which is outside the modelled scope."@en .

aia:ra_recruitment_eurodistribution_distributor a owl:NamedIndividual , aia:RoleAssignment ;
    aia:concernsSystem aia:ExampleRecruitmentScreeningSystem ;
    aia:hasRole        aia:Distributor ;
    aia:heldBy         aia:ExampleActorEuroDistributionBV ;
    skos:prefLabel "EuroDistribution as distributor of the recruitment system"@en ;
    skos:definition """The holding of the distributor role by EuroDistribution BV in respect
        of the recruitment screening system, by making it available on the Union market
        otherwise than as provider or importer."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Art. 3(7). The second of two concurrent assignments held by one actor
        for one system -- Recital 83's example. Obligations at Art. 24, outside scope, so
        CQ3 returns nothing for either role even before its FILTER applies."""@en .

### The imaging triage software ###################################

aia:ra_medical_helvetia_provider a owl:NamedIndividual , aia:RoleAssignment ;
    aia:concernsSystem aia:ExampleMedicalImagingTriageSoftware ;
    aia:hasRole        aia:Provider ;
    aia:heldBy         aia:ExampleActorHelvetiaMedTechAG ;
    skos:prefLabel "Helvetia MedTech as provider of the imaging triage software"@en ;
    skos:definition """The holding of the provider role by Helvetia MedTech AG in respect
        of the imaging triage software, by having developed it and placed it on the
        market under its own name."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Art. 3(3). Terminated by aia:rr_medical_rhine under Art. 25(2)."@en .

aia:ra_medical_rhine_importer a owl:NamedIndividual , aia:RoleAssignment ;
    aia:concernsSystem aia:ExampleMedicalImagingTriageSoftware ;
    aia:hasRole        aia:Importer ;
    aia:heldBy         aia:ExampleActorRhineImportsGmbH ;
    skos:prefLabel "Rhine Imports as importer of the imaging triage software"@en ;
    skos:definition """The holding of the importer role by Rhine Imports GmbH in respect of
        the imaging triage software, by placing on the Union market a system bearing the
        trade mark of a third-country undertaking."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Art. 3(6). Retained after the Art. 25(1)(a) reassignment."@en .

aia:ra_medical_rhine_provider a owl:NamedIndividual , aia:RoleAssignment ;
    aia:concernsSystem aia:ExampleMedicalImagingTriageSoftware ;
    aia:hasRole        aia:Provider ;
    aia:heldBy         aia:ExampleActorRhineImportsGmbH ;
    skos:prefLabel "Rhine Imports as provider of the imaging triage software"@en ;
    skos:definition """The holding of the provider role by Rhine Imports GmbH in respect of
        the imaging triage software, acquired by affixing its own trade mark to a
        high-risk system already placed on the market."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Art. 25(1)(a)."@en .

### The workforce analytics system ################################

aia:ra_workforce_peoplemetrics_distributor a owl:NamedIndividual , aia:RoleAssignment ;
    aia:concernsSystem aia:ExampleWorkforceAnalyticsSystem ;
    aia:hasRole        aia:Distributor ;
    aia:heldBy         aia:ExampleActorPeopleMetricsLtd ;
    skos:prefLabel "PeopleMetrics as distributor of the workforce analytics system"@en ;
    skos:definition """The holding of the distributor role by PeopleMetrics Ltd in respect
        of the workforce analytics system, by making it available on the Union market."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Art. 3(7). Retained after the Art. 25(1)(c) reassignment."@en .

aia:ra_workforce_peoplemetrics_provider a owl:NamedIndividual , aia:RoleAssignment ;
    aia:concernsSystem aia:ExampleWorkforceAnalyticsSystem ;
    aia:hasRole        aia:Provider ;
    aia:heldBy         aia:ExampleActorPeopleMetricsLtd ;
    skos:prefLabel "PeopleMetrics as provider of the workforce analytics system"@en ;
    skos:definition """The holding of the provider role by PeopleMetrics Ltd in respect of
        the workforce analytics system, acquired by modifying the intended purpose of a
        system not classified as high-risk so that it became high-risk."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Art. 25(1)(c)."@en .

#################################################################
#    Article 25(1) reassignment conditions
#
#    General legal content rather than fixture: these are the three
#    circumstances of Art. 25(1) and would move to the core if an
#    Article 25 module were ever built. The worked example is the only
#    file that uses them. All three are used below.
#
#    Conditions carry NO aia:statedIn: that property's domain is the
#    union of aia:Obligation, aia:RoleReassignment and
#    aia:ConformityAssessmentRoute, and adding aia:ReassignmentCondition
#    to it is a change to the core, not to a fixture. The provision is
#    named in rdfs:comment, which is the convention the class skeleton
#    used before article resources existed.
#################################################################

aia:rc_art25_1_a_own_name a owl:NamedIndividual , aia:ReassignmentCondition ;
    skos:prefLabel "Affixing one's own name or trade mark (Art. 25(1)(a))"@en ;
    skos:definition """Putting one's name or trade mark on a high-risk AI system already
        placed on the market or put into service, without prejudice to contractual
        arrangements stipulating that the obligations are otherwise allocated."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Art. 25(1)(a)."@en .

aia:rc_art25_1_b_substantial_modification a owl:NamedIndividual , aia:ReassignmentCondition ;
    rdfs:seeAlso eu-aiact-owl:SubstantialModification ;
    skos:prefLabel "Substantial modification of a high-risk system (Art. 25(1)(b))"@en ;
    skos:definition """Making a substantial modification to a high-risk AI system that has
        already been placed on the market or put into service, in such a way that it remains
        a high-risk AI system pursuant to Article 6."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Art. 25(1)(b). eu-aiact-owl:SubstantialModification carries the
        Art. 3(23) definition and is referenced rather than restated."""@en .

aia:rc_art25_1_c_purpose_modification a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        aia:ReassignmentCondition , aia:AnnexIIIGround , aia:PurposeGround ;
    rdfs:seeAlso eu-aiact-owl:HighRiskAISystem-AnnexIII-4-b ;
    skos:prefLabel "Modification of intended purpose making a system high-risk (Art. 25(1)(c))"@en ;
    skos:definition """Modifying the intended purpose of an AI system, including a
        general-purpose AI system, which has not been classified as high-risk and has
        already been placed on the market or put into service, in such a way that the
        system concerned becomes a high-risk AI system in accordance with Article 6."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Art. 25(1)(c), and THE INDIVIDUAL THAT JUSTIFIES AN OMISSION FROM THE
        DISJOINTNESS AXIOM. It is a reassignment condition and a classification ground at
        once: the modification is both the conduct that promotes the distributor to
        provider and the fact in virtue of which the system becomes high-risk. It is used in
        both positions below -- as aia:triggeredBy on the reassignment and as
        aia:classifiedOnGround on the system. Typed AnnexIIIGround as well as PurposeGround
        because Art. 6(2) reaches the category through the Annex III use case, which is what
        aia:HighRiskByGround has a disjunct for; the purpose typing alone would not
        classify."""@en .

#################################################################
#    Role reassignments, Article 25
#
#    Three events, one per limb of Art. 25(1), each deliberately
#    ASYMMETRIC: aia:promotes does not end the prior assignment,
#    aia:terminates does end the initial provider's.
#################################################################

aia:rr_recruitment_northborough a owl:NamedIndividual , aia:RoleReassignment ;
    aia:concernsSystem aia:ExampleRecruitmentScreeningSystem ;
    aia:triggeredBy    aia:rc_art25_1_b_substantial_modification ;
    aia:promotes       aia:ra_recruitment_northborough_deployer ;
    aia:establishes    aia:ra_recruitment_northborough_provider ;
    aia:terminates     aia:ra_recruitment_talentflow_provider ;
    aia:statedIn       aia:art_25 ;
    skos:prefLabel "North Borough Council becomes provider of the recruitment system"@en ;
    skos:definition """The event by which North Borough Council, having substantially
        modified the recruitment screening system while it remained high-risk, came to be
        considered its provider, while TalentFlow GmbH ceased to be."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Art. 25(1)(b) and 25(2). The deployer assignment is promoted and
        RETAINED; the initial provider's is terminated. That asymmetry is the substantive
        content of the event and is why aia:promotes and aia:terminates are two
        properties."""@en .

aia:rr_medical_rhine a owl:NamedIndividual , aia:RoleReassignment ;
    aia:concernsSystem aia:ExampleMedicalImagingTriageSoftware ;
    aia:triggeredBy    aia:rc_art25_1_a_own_name ;
    aia:promotes       aia:ra_medical_rhine_importer ;
    aia:establishes    aia:ra_medical_rhine_provider ;
    aia:terminates     aia:ra_medical_helvetia_provider ;
    aia:statedIn       aia:art_25 ;
    skos:prefLabel "Rhine Imports becomes provider of the imaging triage software"@en ;
    skos:definition """The event by which Rhine Imports GmbH, having affixed its own trade
        mark to a high-risk system already placed on the market, came to be considered its
        provider, while Helvetia MedTech AG ceased to be."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Art. 25(1)(a) and 25(2). Promotion from importer rather than deployer."@en .

aia:rr_workforce_peoplemetrics a owl:NamedIndividual , aia:RoleReassignment ;
    aia:concernsSystem aia:ExampleWorkforceAnalyticsSystem ;
    aia:triggeredBy    aia:rc_art25_1_c_purpose_modification ;
    aia:promotes       aia:ra_workforce_peoplemetrics_distributor ;
    aia:establishes    aia:ra_workforce_peoplemetrics_provider ;
    aia:statedIn       aia:art_25 ;
    skos:prefLabel "PeopleMetrics becomes provider of the workforce analytics system"@en ;
    skos:definition """The event by which PeopleMetrics Ltd, having modified the intended
        purpose of a system not classified as high-risk so that it became high-risk, came to
        be considered its provider."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Art. 25(1)(c). NO aia:terminates, and the absence is deliberate: the
        example graph records no provider assignment for this system, so there is no
        assignment to terminate. Art. 25(2) would apply to whoever initially placed it on
        the market, and that party is simply not in the fixture. This is also what leaves
        CQ4's OPTIONAL unbound on one of its three rows, showing the OPTIONAL is
        load-bearing."""@en .

#################################################################
#    Oversight assignments, Articles 70 and 74
#
#    Four, each pairing one obligation with one authority. The pairings
#    are not exhaustive and are not meant to be: they are the ones the
#    Act names a supervisory competence for in terms.
#
#    NO AI OFFICE ASSIGNMENT. CQ5's VALUES clause admits
#    eu-aiact:AIOffice and nothing binds it. Art. 75(1) makes the AI
#    Office exclusively competent for AI systems based on a
#    general-purpose AI model where model and system come from the same
#    provider, and for systems that are or are integrated into a very
#    large online platform or search engine; its competence over the
#    models themselves lies in Chapter V, out of scope under decision 2
#    in ../reports/STATUS.md. No example system falls under Art. 75(1),
#    so an assignment here would assert a competence the Act does not
#    give it over these systems.
#################################################################

aia:ExampleNationalCompetentAuthority a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        eu-aiact-owl:NationalCompetentAuthority , org:Organization ;
    skos:prefLabel "National Competent Authority of Member State A (example authority)"@en ;
    skos:definition """The notifying authority and market surveillance authority designated
        or established by a Member State for the purposes of the Regulation."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Art. 3(48), Art. 70."@en .

aia:ExampleMarketSurveillanceAuthority a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        eu-aiact-owl:MarketSurveillanceAuthority , org:Organization ;
    skos:prefLabel "Market Surveillance Authority of Member State A (example authority)"@en ;
    skos:definition """The authority carrying out the activities and taking the measures
        pursuant to Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 in respect of AI systems."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Art. 3(26), Art. 74. NOTE FOR CQ5: eu-aiact makes
        MarketSurveillanceAuthority a SUBCLASS of NationalCompetentAuthority, which is
        faithful to Art. 3(48), so over an inferred graph this individual matches two of
        CQ5's four VALUES types and is returned on two rows per obligation. That is the
        import's taxonomy showing through, not duplicate data."""@en .

aia:ExampleNotifiedBody a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        eu-aiact-owl:NotifiedBody , org:Organization ;
    skos:prefLabel "Notified Body 0001 (example body)"@en ;
    skos:definition """A conformity assessment body notified in accordance with the
        Regulation and the applicable Union harmonisation legislation."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Art. 3(22). Descends from eu-aiact:ConformityAssessmentBody and not from
        dpv-owl:Authority, which is why aia:assignedTo carries a union range."""@en .

aia:oa_art16_k_nca a owl:NamedIndividual , aia:OversightAssignment ;
    aia:oversees   aia:ob_art16_k ;
    aia:assignedTo aia:ExampleNationalCompetentAuthority ;
    skos:prefLabel "National competent authority supervises the duty to demonstrate conformity"@en ;
    skos:definition """The supervision by the national competent authority of the provider's
        duty to demonstrate, upon reasoned request, the conformity of a high-risk AI system
        with the requirements of Section 2."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Art. 16(k) with Art. 21. The core file already records this as the duty
        CQ5 pairs with an oversight assignment."""@en .

aia:oa_art16_f_notified a owl:NamedIndividual , aia:OversightAssignment ;
    aia:oversees   aia:ob_art16_f ;
    aia:assignedTo aia:ExampleNotifiedBody ;
    skos:prefLabel "Notified body supervises the conformity assessment duty"@en ;
    skos:definition """The involvement of a notified body in the conformity assessment
        procedure a provider must ensure the high-risk AI system undergoes before it is
        placed on the market."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Art. 16(f) with Art. 43. The notified body is the third party of the
        Annex VII route, which is why this obligation is also the one both conformity
        assessment routes attach to."""@en .

aia:oa_art26_5_msa a owl:NamedIndividual , aia:OversightAssignment ;
    aia:oversees   aia:ob_art26_5 ;
    aia:assignedTo aia:ExampleMarketSurveillanceAuthority ;
    skos:prefLabel "Market surveillance authority supervises deployer monitoring and reporting"@en ;
    skos:definition """The supervision by the market surveillance authority of the deployer's
        duty to monitor the operation of a high-risk AI system and to inform the provider
        and the authority of risks and serious incidents."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Art. 26(5) with Arts. 73, 74 and 79(1)."@en .

aia:oa_art26_12_msa a owl:NamedIndividual , aia:OversightAssignment ;
    aia:oversees   aia:ob_art26_12 ;
    aia:assignedTo aia:ExampleMarketSurveillanceAuthority ;
    skos:prefLabel "Market surveillance authority supervises deployer cooperation"@en ;
    skos:definition """The supervision by the market surveillance authority of the deployer's
        duty to cooperate with the competent authorities in any action those authorities take
        in relation to a high-risk AI system."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Art. 26(12) with Art. 74."@en .

#################################################################
#    Conformity assessment routes, Article 43
#
#    All three attach to Art. 16(f), the duty to ensure the system
#    undergoes the relevant procedure. They are alternatives, so CQ5
#    returns that obligation on three rows -- which is the point: the
#    route is a CHOICE, and eu-aiact has no term for the choice, only
#    for the assessment. Which one applies depends on the ground:
#    Annex VI or VII for Annex III systems under Art. 43(1)-(2), and the
#    sectoral procedure for Annex I, Section A systems under Art. 43(3),
#    including those that also fall within Annex III.
#
#    A LIMIT OF CQ5, VISIBLE ONLY ONCE THE DATA EXISTS. CQ5's question
#    asks which route applies to a given high-risk AI SYSTEM, but the
#    query binds a route to an OBLIGATION and no property relates a
#    route to a system. The question's second half is therefore
#    answered only obligation-indexed. Recorded in ../reports/cq-results.md
#    rather than patched here, because adding aia:appliesToSystem would
#    be a change to the core that no query in ../queries/ binds.
#################################################################

aia:route_annex_VI a owl:NamedIndividual , aia:ConformityAssessmentRoute ;
    aia:appliesToObligation aia:ob_art16_f ;
    aia:statedIn            aia:annex_VI ;
    skos:prefLabel "Internal control route (Annex VI)"@en ;
    skos:definition """The conformity assessment procedure based on internal control, in
        which the provider itself verifies that its quality management system and the
        technical documentation conform and that the system meets the Section 2
        requirements."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Art. 43 and Annex VI."@en .

aia:route_annex_VII a owl:NamedIndividual , aia:ConformityAssessmentRoute ;
    aia:appliesToObligation aia:ob_art16_f ;
    aia:statedIn            aia:annex_VII ;
    skos:prefLabel "Quality management system and technical documentation route (Annex VII)"@en ;
    skos:definition """The conformity assessment procedure in which a notified body assesses
        the quality management system and the technical documentation of the high-risk AI
        system."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Art. 43 and Annex VII. The route on which aia:oa_art16_f_notified's
        notified body acts."""@en .

aia:route_annex_I_sectoral a owl:NamedIndividual , aia:ConformityAssessmentRoute ;
    aia:appliesToObligation aia:ob_art16_f ;
    aia:statedIn            aia:art_43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "Sectoral procedure under Annex I, Section A legislation (Art. 43(3))"@en ;
    skos:definition """The conformity assessment procedure required by the Union harmonisation
        legislation listed in Annex I, Section A that covers the product, into which the
        Section 2 requirements and the assessment of the Article 17 quality management system
        are incorporated, with points 3, 4.3, 4.4, 4.5, the fifth paragraph of point 4.6 and
        point 5 of Annex VII applying. It also applies where the system additionally falls
        within an Annex III category."""@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Art. 43(3), verified against the Official Journal. The route of
        aia:ExampleMedicalImagingTriageSoftware, whose notified body under Regulation (EU)
        2017/745 carries out the assessment."""@en .
